  "contracts": {
    "pan": "With measurement+0x571 active,0x50abe8..0x50ac64 and0x50adc0..0x50ae3c compare retained right wavelength+0x549<=maximum+0x472 AND retained left+0x553>=minimum+0x468. If either fails both shoulder X+0x545/+0x541 become0;otherwise both Xreproject from retained wavelength/new step. The pair-failure branches do not clear shoulder Y+0x53d/+0x539 or Extended wavelength/continuum values. Endpoints are inclusive in this finite ordered branch.",
    "zoomReset": "0x50a854..0x50a896,0x50aa60..0x50aaa2 and0x50af58..0x50af9a reproject both stored shoulder wavelengths to Xwhen active,then call repaint0x507dc4. Center projection differs between zoom directions/reset.",
    "paint": "0x5081e4..0x5081f2 invokes global center painting then shoulder painting. Center painting0x509cf4 invokes0x5096dc only if centerX>0;revalidation can clear shoulder XandY,then shoulder painter uses positive Xflags. Therefore scalar retention is not unconditional native visual or confirmation recovery."
  },
  "implemented": [
    "Bounded paired-pan paint predicate for a complete valid manual region with known comparison-pane origin and actual selected-source association;numeric/unbound/partial regions retain prior independent projection. Repaint/Inspect/reverse/resize/scroll alone retain an unchanged paint snapshot.",
    "Pure atomic window/paint transitions preserve consecutive pan updates and no-op zoom;the immutable presentation snapshot binds exact source choice,context,marker point/pane,all draft strings,mark revision and actual viewport identity. Any new manual mark,numeric/source/context/window change retires it;new pan recomputes it.",
    "Both shoulder stems/endpoints and connector hide together when either retained endpoint lies outside the panned window. Global/center mark remains subject to existing geometric clipping. Numeric strings,confirmed records,source flux/counts/seed,integrator and all formats unchanged.",
    "Zoom/reset continue existing continuous SVG reconstruction from retained numeric values. Active-source full-range labelled fallbacks are excluded from the paired-window policy.",
    "Known pane origin substitutes for native active-modal flag;continuous coordinates and explicit mark revision/reconstruction are browser policies. This does not add native pixel/sentinel/Yflag state or claim a fully ported zoom/repaint lifecycle.",
    "Existing numeric Calculate remains available when a painted pair hides. Native coordinate-zero confirmation gate and scalar/Yflag distinction remain separate unported contracts;this change does not silently alter result eligibility."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Exact native integerX/Y,positive-Xsentinels,rounded-center/order revalidation and asymmetriczoom/reset/readout/event lifecycle",
    "Native coordinate-zero confirmation gate versus retained Extended fields and complete modal/reentry behavior",
    "Automatic combined-bottom source after forced trace entry remains unresolved;explicit Unknown selection retained",
    "GDI/x87/runtime,wider numerical domains,result/grade/legacy interchange,broader edition/classroom/rights gates"
  ],
  "uncertainty": "Read-only static intent and declared browser paint policy. No original execution/emulation or original runtime oracle;source credits/license uncertainties retained."
}
